ST4 License
===========

ST4 is an Atari ST compression project: a split-stream, unit-aligned data
format for the plain 68000, grown out of ST1 (https://github.com/odipar/ST1)
and, through it, the ZX1 data compression format. It contains the ST4 68000
decompressors, the supporting Java st4 and C# nt4 tools and reference
implementations, and the YMX chiptune player. It follows the dual licensing
structure of the original ZX1 (https://github.com/einar-saukas/ZX1) and of
ST1, whose license this is:

1. THE COMPRESSOR - the Java and C# compressors and optimizers (St4Block,
   St4Optimizer, St4FastOptimizer, St4EventOptimizer, St4Compressor, Java
   St4, and the C# Nt4 counterparts), derived from Einar Saukas' optimal C
   compressor through ST1's jx1 - is available under the BSD 3-Clause License
   below. In practice this is relevant only if you modify its source code
   and/or incorporate the compressor within your own products; if you just
   execute it to compress files, you can simply ignore these conditions.

2. THE DECOMPRESSORS - Java St4Decompressor/Dst4, the C# Decompressor/Dnt4
   counterparts, the ST4 decompressors in 68k/ (ST4.S, ST4_wrap.S, and
   ST4_ring.S), and the YMX chiptune player in ymx/ (YMX.S and YMX_player.S)
   - can be used freely within your own programs (for any platform), even for
   commercial releases. The only condition is that you must indicate somehow
   in your documentation that you have used ZX1, via ST4, st4, or nt4.

Attribution
-----------

* The ZX1 data compression format and algorithm was designed and implemented
  by Einar Saukas (Copyright (c) 2021), with thanks to introspec/spke. The
  original C and z80 sources live in the ZX1 repository and, vendored, in
  odipar/ST1 under c/zx1/.
* The ST4 format (the four streams, the unit alignment, the container) and
  the differences from ST1 and ZX1 - see README.md - are Copyright (c) 2026
  Robbert van Dalen.
* The Java tools, the C# nt4 port, the ST4 68000 decompressors, the YMX
  chiptune packer and player, and the emulation/measurement rigs were written
  by Claude (Anthropic's Claude Code) under the direction of Robbert van
  Dalen. ST4_wrap.S is based on ST1_wrap.S, which was written for ST1 by
  OpenAI Codex.
* The YM6 register-dump format is by Arnaud Carré (Leonard/Oxygene); YMX reads
  it and is inspired by Steve Clarets' MinYMiser player. The LHA depacker in
  org.ym6 is ported from the ST-Sound library's LZH code by Arnaud Carré,
  itself based on LZH code by Haruhiko Okumura (1991) and Kerwin F. Medina
  (1996).

